[methods]  nu treatment for this run
  tlasso    (run_tlasso)
      nu   : FIXED at nu = 3, not estimated
      args : n_iter=200, verbose=False, tol=1e-05
  t*lasso   (run_tstar_varlasso)
      nu   : FIXED at nu = 3, not estimated
      args : n_iter=200, verbose=False, tol=1e-05
  t+lasso   (run_em_diagonal)
      nu   : ESTIMATED per coordinate (nu_j), bracket [0.0001, 100], nu_j = 0 meaning that coordinate went Gaussian
      args : n_iter=200, verbose=False, tol=1e-05
  glasso    (graphical_lasso)
      nu   : not a parameter of this model
      args : max_iter=2000, verbose=False
  ~t+lasso  (run_em_exact)
      nu   : ESTIMATED per coordinate (nu_j), bracket [0.0001, 100], nu_j = 0 meaning that coordinate went Gaussian
      args : n_iter=200, verbose=False, tol=1e-05
  Reading the per-rho nu lines below: tlasso and t*lasso print a scalar `nu`,
  run_em_diagonal a `median nu`/`median eta` over coordinates. The two nu's are NOT
  comparable -- tau ~ Gamma(nu/2, nu/2) for the t models, so small nu is the heavy
  tail, while EM_algorithm's tau_j ~ Inv-Gamma(2/nu_j, 2/nu_j) puts the heavy tail at
  large nu_j.
